<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jerónimo de Albuquerque</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1510–1584</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jerónimo de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-de-albuquerque">Albuquerque</a> was a Portuguese nobleman in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, the brother-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duarte-coelho">Duarte Coelho</a>, first donatary of the Captaincy of Pernambuco. He governed the captaincy for long periods during the absence and minority of its heirs, fighting the Indigenous peoples and promoting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> plantations. He had many children with his Tabajara wife, Maria do Espírito Santo Arcoverde, and is known as the patriarch of many Pernambucan families.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jeronimo-de-albuquerque.jpg" alt="Jerónimo de Albuquerque" width="196" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GabrielSampaio27 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jer%C3%B4nimo_de_Albuquerque.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
